Subject: [PATCH] HID: spi-hid: propagate supply lookup errors

Every error from devm_regulator_get_optional() other than -ENODEV was
turned into -EPROBE_DEFER, so a real failure deferred forever without a
message. Return the actual error through dev_err_probe(), which still
defers quietly when the supply is not ready yet.
---
diff --git a/drivers/hid/spi-hid/spi-hid-core.c b/drivers/hid/spi-hid/spi-hid-core.c
index 17eefe2..821f8c8 100644
--- a/drivers/hid/spi-hid/spi-hid-core.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/spi-hid/spi-hid-core.c
@@ -1284,8 +1284,10 @@ static int spi_hid_probe(struct spi_device *spi)
 
 	shid->supply = devm_regulator_get_optional(dev, "vdd");
 	if (IS_ERR(shid->supply)) {
-		if (PTR_ERR(shid->supply) != -ENODEV) {
-			ret = -EPROBE_DEFER;
+		ret = PTR_ERR(shid->supply);
+		/* Only a missing supply is optional; defer or fail otherwise. */
+		if (ret != -ENODEV) {
+			dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "Failed to get vdd supply\n");
 			goto err_sysfs;
 		}
 		shid->supply = NULL;
